,249)from CHF 30 Price varies by group size L161: 【96†Special Offer This isn't just another sightseeing tour—it's a private, expertly guided journey through Egypt’s most iconic landmarks, curated to offer comfort, insight, and unforgettable memories in a single day. Skip the crowds and rigid itineraries of group tours. With your own Egyptologist guide and private vehicle, you'll explore the Pyramids of Giza at your own pace, stand face-to-face with the Great Sphinx, and uncover ancient secrets at the Valley Temple.\nL162: Next, step into the world’s largest archaeological museum—the Grand Egyptian Museum (GEM)—and see King Tutankhamun’s treasures and thousands of artifacts in a state-of-the-art setting. To end the day, unwind with a peaceful 1-hour sail on a traditional felucca boat along the Nile River—one of the most magical ways to see Cairo from the water.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSagrada Familia Skip-the-Line and Guided Tour 2026 - Barcelona - BOOK NOW (https://www.viator.com/tours/Barcelona/Sagrada-Familia-Skip-The-Line-Tour/d562-340934P4)\nciteturn3view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.viator.com/tours/Barcelona/Sagrada-Familia-Skip-The-Line-Tour/d562-340934P4\",\"lineno\":220}); Total lines: 1199\nL190: ##\nL191: \nL192: Explore our promoted experiences\nL193: \nL194: cite100†Barcelona, Spain 3.3(7)Private Barcelona Jewish Quarter Tour with Local Expert Guide from CHF 142 Price varies by group size L195: \nL196: cite101†Barcelona, Spain TOP Barcelona : Private guided tour with your mobile from CHF 10 L197: \nL198: cite102†Barcelona, Spain 5.0(3)Barcelona Private Car Tour with Hidden Gems and Landmarks from CHF 238 Per group L199: \nL200: cite103†Barcelona, Spain 4.9(86)Sagrada Familia Tour: Gaudí’s Secrets from CHF 5 L201: cite104†Barcelona, Spain 4.8(18)Private Complete Barcelona Walking Tour with Local Guide from CHF 238 Per group L202: \nL203: cite105†Barcelona, Spain 5.0(73)Barcelona Walking Tour: Sagrada Familia, Gaudi and Gothic Quarter from CHF 23 L204: \nL205: cite106†Barcelona, Spain 5.0(100)Barcelona Essential Highlights: Private Bike Tour from CHF 38 L206: \nL207: cite107†Barcelona, Spain 4.9(40)Best of Barcelona Highlights: Private Half-Day E-Bike Tour from CHF 76 Price varies by group size L208: \nL209: cite108†Viator earns higher commissions on experiences featured here L210: ## Overview\nL211: \nL212: There’s no need to fret about never-ending ticket lines for the Sagrada Familia. Instead, make your visit hassle-free by opting for this guided tour, which includes skip-the-line entry. As well as learning about the history of this magnificent building, you can also have the opportunity to look at some of Gaudi’s original sketches.\nL213: \nL214:   * Explore the Sagrada Familia with a guide to provide commentary\nL215: \nL216:   * Skip the long lines and get inside quickly\nL217:   * Audio headsets provided for groups of 9 or more\nL218: \nL219:   * Lots to see—including hand-drawn illustrations and artifacts\nL220: ## What's Included\nL221: \nL222:   * Skip-the-line Sagrada Familia Tickets\nL223: \nL224:   * Sagrada Familia Guided Tour\nL225: \nL226:   * Certified Tour Guide from Barcelona Tourism Authority\nL227: \nL228:   * Audio headset for groups of 9+ people\nL229: \nL230:   * Private transportation\nL231: \nL232:   * Access to the towers\nL233: \nL234: See 1 More\nL235: \nL236: ## Meeting and Pickup\nL237: ### Meeting point\nL238: \nL239:   * Carrer de Mallorca, 418, Eixample, 08013 Barcelona, Spain\nL240: \nL241: Open in Google Maps\nL242: \nL243: Find your guide holding a Golden Tour Guide sign inside Ringels souvenir shop at C/ de Mallorca, 418, 08013 Barcelona. Please be there 15 minutes before the tour starts.\nL244: \nL245: ### End point\nL246: \nL247:   * Sagrada Família, Eixample, Barcelona, Spain\nL248: \nL249: Open in Google Maps\nL250: \nL251: The tour will end inside Sagrada Familia.\nL252: \nL253: ## Itinerary\nL254: \nL255: 1\nL256: \nL257: ### Basilica de la Sagrada Familia\nL258: \nL259: 1 hour 30 minutes • Admission Ticket Included\nL260: ## Additional Info\nL261: \nL262:   * Confirmation will be received at time of booking\nL263: \nL264:   * Not wheelchair accessible\nL265: \nL266:   * Near public transportation\nL267: \nL268:   * Most travelers can participate\nL269:   * It is difficult to anticipate when La Sagrada Familia will be crowded. Typically, major attractions experience long queues during peak travel periods such as summer, weekends, Christmas, Easter, and local holidays. By purchasing a skip-the-line ticket, you can bypass the queue if there happens to be one. Unfortunately, it is impossible to predict specific days and times when lines are likely to form.\nL270:   * To ensure safety, all visitors are required to pass through metal detectors at the security checkpoint. Please anticipate a wait time of approximately 20-30 minutes to clear security.\nL271: \nL272:   * In order to enter the Sagrada Familia Basilica, visitors are expected to dress appropriately as it is a Catholic church. Tank tops, strapless shirts, short shorts, or sandals are not permitted. Additionally, visitors are not permitted to enter the church wearing clothing intended for celebrations or festivities.\nL273:   * Please arrive at the meeting point 15 minutes prior to the scheduled departure time.\nL274: \nL275:   * Customers must bring an ID to prove their age. If you cannot show the correct proof of age, Sagrada Familia will not allow entry, and you won't be able to get a refund.\nL276: \nL277:   * Audio headsets are provided for groups of 10 or more participants\nL278: \nL279:   * This tour/activity will have a maximum of 30 travelers\nL280: \nL281: Show 5 more\nL282: \nL283: Supplied by [Button: Golden Tour Guide]\nL284: ## Cancellation Policy\nL285: \nL286: You can cancel up to 24 hours in advance of the experience for a full refund.\nL287: \nL288: Show more\nL289: \nL290: ## Questions?\nL291: \nL292: Visit the Viator Help Centre for any further questions.\nL293: \nL294: Product code: 340934P4\nL295: \nL296: Viator Help Center\nL297: ## Traveler Photos\nL298: \nL299: cite109†Image: Gallery picture 1 (from a traveler's review)†media.tacdn.com L300: \nL301: cite110†Image: Gallery picture 2 (from a traveler's review)†media.tacdn.com L302: \nL303: cite111†Image: Gallery picture 3 (from a traveler's review)†media.tacdn.com L304: \nL305: cite112†Image: Gallery picture 4 (from a traveler's review)†media.tacdn.com L306: \nL307: cite113†Image: Gallery picture 5 (from a traveler's review)†media.tacdn.com See more\nL308: ## Reviews\nL309: \nL310: 4.7\nL311: \nL312: based on 4,616 reviews\nL313: \nL314: Total reviews and rating from Viator & Tripadvisor\nL315: \nL316: 5 stars\nL317: \nL318: 3920\nL319: \nL320: 4 stars\nL321: \nL322: 345\nL323: \nL324: 3 stars\nL325: \nL326: 149\nL327: \nL328: 2 stars\nL329: \nL330: 70\nL331: \nL332: 1 star\nL333: \nL334: 132\nL335: \nL336: cite108†We perform checks on reviews L337: \nL338: [Input: Search reviews (e.g. guide)]\nL339: \nL340: Sort by: Most insightful\nL341: \nL342: [Input]\nL343: \nL344: [Input]\nL345: \nL346: ### Sagrada Familia\nL347: \nL348: JamesE_K, Oct 2026\nL349: \nL350: Olga E did a fabulous tour of the Sagrada. She was so passionate and knowledgable about Gaudi and his masterpiece!\nL351: #### Response from Host, Oct 2026\nL352: \nL353: Thank you for your fantastic 5-star review! We’re delighted you enjoyed exploring Sagrada Família in Barcelona with Golden Tour Guide. It’s wonderful to hear that Olga E’s passion and deep knowledge of Gaudí brought this extraordinary masterpiece to life. We’ll be sure to share your lovely feedback with her!\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nViator (https://www.viator.com/support/siteoperation)\nciteturn3view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.viator.com/support/siteoperation\",\"lineno\":225}); Total lines: 279\nL192:     * cite153†Outdoor Activities L193:     * cite154†Seasonal & Special Occasions L194:     * cite155†Wildlife Watching L195:     * cite156†Wine, Beer & Spirits L196:     * cite157†Winter Sports L197:   * Trending articles\nL198:     * cite158†11 Charming Small Towns To Visit in New England L199:     * cite159†Where to See Fall Foliage in Boston L200:     * cite160†13 Witchy Haunts Around the World L201:     * cite161†Visiting Kyoto For the First Time? Here’s What to See and Do L202:     * cite162†10 of the Top Native and Indigenous Experiences in the US, According to Viator Travelers L203:     * cite163†Haunted Salem: A Spooky City Guide to Salem L204:   * cite164†Read the Viator blog L205: # How Viator works\nL206: \nL207: 1. Introduction\nL208: \nL209: When you book an Experience, Viator, Inc. (“Viator”) provides the Platform, but not the Experience itself. Viator is a company incorporated under the laws of Delaware, USA, with its place of business located at 400 1st Avenue, Needham, MA 02494, USA.\nL210: \nL211: Some of the words you’ll see on this page have specific meanings, so please check the definitions in the cite165†Viator Terms of Use .\nL212: \nL213: 2. What does Viator do?\nL214: \nL215: We provide a place for you to discover and book Experiences.\nL216: When you make a Booking on our Platform, you enter into a contract with the Supplier—i.e. the person or entity selling the Experience to you, who is responsible for providing the Experience.\nL217: Before being listed, Suppliers enter into a contract with Viator to allow Viator to promote and make those Experiences available for booking on Viator’s site and through Viator’s third party distribution channels. Experiences must meet Viator's cite166†Acceptance Criteria†help.supplier.viator.com and cite167†Quality Standards†help.supplier.viator.com to be listed, and stay listed, on the Platform.\nL218: Viator may charge a non-refundable fee to review a new Experience submitted by a Supplier to be listed in accordance with the Acceptance Criteria and Quality Standards.\nL219: The Experiences you see displayed on the Platform are not reflective of all the experiences available either online or offline.\nL220: \nL221: 3. How does Viator make money?\nL222: \nL223: We don’t sell any Experiences, and we don’t own any of the businesses you see listed on our site. When you make a Booking, the Supplier pays Viator a commission after you’ve had the Experience.\nL224: \nL225: 4. Our approach to searching, sorting, ranking, and recommending\nL226: We use various systems on the Platform to rank and recommend Experiences, to allow you to search for Experiences, and to sort and order what you see (we’ll refer to them as “Systems” here). We use Systems to present information on the Platform to help you discover Experiences we think you’ll enjoy.\nL227: \nL228: Search list pages\nL229: We offer you the ability to search for Experiences, and we provide recommendations based on what you input into the search box, for example a geographical location. In presenting you with a list based on your search, we may sometimes also use information we have gathered based on how you interact with the Platform, including but not limited to your past searches on the Platform, or how you navigated to the Platform (for example, if you arrived on our site through a search engine).\nL230: When listings first appear as a result of a search, they will be sorted in a default order which may be labeled “Featured.” This default sort order recommends Experiences using a System that takes into account some or all of the following, depending on a range of factors including how you search and select a destination, and whether you filter your search: relevance, quality (assessed against Viator’s Quality Standards), reviews, ratings, photographs (quality and quantity), popularity, availability, pricing, bookings made through Viator, and payments made to Viator by Suppliers.\nL231: We might also personalize the search results based on Experiences you have browsed or booked in the recent past or on indicators of your current location.\nL232: Many of the above factors help the Systems decide which Experiences might be the most interesting and relevant to you. Some play a small role in that decision, while others play a big role, and the importance of each factor can change, depending on the features of the Experience, how you and other people use the Platform, and our analysis of how effective we are in showing you the best selection of Experiences.\nL233: Notwithstanding those changes, the factors that most often carry the most weight are relevance, Viator's revenue, and booking volume.\nL234: If you would prefer that we show you Experiences based on different parameters, you can sort results in other ways, which might include:\nL235:   * Traveler rating: Experiences are shown in order of popularity based on the Experience’s overall rating, calculated using reviews and ratings submitted on both Viator and Tripadvisor.\nL236:   * Price: You can choose to see Experiences listed by lowest or highest price first.\nL237:   * Duration: Experiences can be ordered in accordance with their duration—either the longest or the shortest first.\nL238:   * New on Viator: Experiences are ranked by the date they were activated on the Viator site, with the newest displayed first.\nL239: Whichever way you choose to order your results, you’ll be able to narrow them down using different filters, which might include some or all of these:\nL240:   * Category: You can pick bus tours, water tours, museum tickets, or one of many other options.\nL241:   * Theme: You could choose to see Experiences that fall within a broad theme such as Food & Drink, Outdoor Activities, or Art & Culture.\nL242:   * Time: Select Experiences that only take place in the morning, or afternoon, or at night.\nL243:   * Price: Set a price range if you only want to see Experiences that fit within that budget. You can also choose to filter by Deals & Discounts if you want to see what special offers are available.\n"
